 ## Residual risks and blockers
 
-- Validator 001 proved that enumerable string-key checks are not a strict closed-input boundary: symbol, non-enumerable, and accessor fields were admitted, including an accessor invoked three times. Corrected admission must inspect descriptors before reading values.
-- Validator 001's `allowed_paths:["../escape"]` probe returned a `START_FAILED/null/SUBJECT_MISMATCH` receipt after entering snapshot/Git work. The contract requires immediate `INPUT_INVALID`, no receipt, and admission before realpath/Git/snapshot/process for every invalid scope grammar class. Public traps prove the diagnosable failure frontier and no Test-observable later effect; structural Test and Validator review prove the internal ordering without claiming read-only syscall counts from the public result.
-- Current timeout sends one `SIGTERM` but resolves only on `error` or `close`; a child handling that signal can keep the producer pending. The approved clarification uses exactly one direct `SIGKILL` when the timer wins, then awaits close and runs post-snapshot. It adds no grace timer, retry, recovery, second child, process-group interface, or caller configuration.
-- The Test's outer watchdog marks an unconditional failure if production does not settle; any rescue kill occurs only in `finally` against the exact ready PID. It cannot be passed into or treated as production authority.
